+
+Native source finding
+---------------------
+
+For ``source_finder = hebog``, the existing Prefect filter task calls the
+optional ``execution.image.hebog_filter`` module in-process, on a
+Rapthor-owned thread executor, then LSMTool. The module owns memory admission,
+sized from Hebog's source-count estimate for the image, blank handling and
+dual-run comparison; ``image.outputs`` keeps subprocess execution for PyBDSF,
+typed refusals and memory too small for the analysis. Hebog owns scientific products and
+imports no Rapthor, Prefect or LSMTool. The current one-task-per-worker layout
+remains unchanged; a distributed Hebog subgraph needs a later layout change.
diff --git a/docs/source/parset.rst b/docs/source/parset.rst
index b40caa2b..8a2ca230 100644
--- a/docs/source/parset.rst
+++ b/docs/source/parset.rst
@@ -1065,3 +1065,61 @@ for how these options are used.
         :term:`generate_initial_skymodel` = ``True``. If photometry and/or astrometry
         skymodels are not provided, then these will not be downloaded and the image
         diagnostics will not be generated.
+
+Native Hebog source finding (experimental)
+------------------------------------------
+
+Install the optional ``rapthor[hebog]`` dependency on Python 3.12 or newer;
+it installs Hebog 0.22 or a later 0.x release from PyPI. Hebog is
+experimental and its releases can change results, so pin the version you
+have checked. Set ``source_finder = hebog`` in ``[imaging]``. PyBDSF remains
+the default and runs in its existing subprocess; Hebog runs inside the
+Prefect filter task.
+
+The current integration requires one single-threaded Dask worker per node.
+Each filter task occupies that worker's only task slot and creates a
+``ThreadExecutor`` capped by ``filter_skymodel_ncores``, ``max_threads`` and
+``cpus_per_task`` when set. Native numerical-library pools are limited to one
+thread for the call and restored afterwards. Do not run multiple such workers
+on one node with overlapping core or memory allocations. The distributed
+Hebog task path on a multi-slot layout is not implemented here.
+
+The task reserves ``hebog.analysis_memory_bytes`` for the sources
+``hebog.expected_source_count`` estimates from the detection image at
+``threshpix``, then admits tile tasks only into the memory left after that
+estimate and the process's current RSS. The budget is the smaller of the
+worker's memory limit and a nonzero ``mem_per_node_gb``. In synchronous
+execution, available machine memory and container/process limits also bound
+it. The estimate counts the image's local maxima ``threshpix`` times the noise
+above the background, so it errs high; peeled sources are not in the image and
+reserve nothing. If no memory remains for the tile tasks, or one needs more
+than remains, the task runs PyBDSF instead. An invalid worker layout fails the
+task.
+
+The following ``[imaging]`` settings apply only to the native backend:
+
+* ``hebog_profile = compact`` (default), or ``continuum``.
+* ``hebog_background = zero`` (default), or ``estimated``.
+* ``hebog_dual_run = False`` (default). If true, both finders run and Hebog's
+  products are selected. Their complete product sets remain in separate
+  directories under ``<root>.source-finders/``. The ordinary image diagnostics
+  include the comparison, exact file hashes, finder selection and admission
+  estimates, so normal diagnostics/restart handling retains them.
+
+The defaults, Hebog's compact profile with PyBDSF's zero mean map, are the
+combination whose island mask made LSMTool keep the same sky-model components
+as PyBDSF's most often in Hebog's comparison. No combination is scientifically
+qualified for Rapthor yet.
+Dual-run differences are observations, not an automatic acceptance decision.
+Both backends use the flat image for detection when no beam Measurement Set is
+given; otherwise they use the true-sky image. LSMTool still filters, groups and
+transfers component names. A no-island result uses LSMTool's negligible dummy
+component; an all-blank image uses Rapthor's existing header-only models and
+placeholder RMS copies.
+
+A typed Hebog ``SourceFinderError`` or ``ExecutorAdmissionError`` invokes the
+PyBDSF subprocess and records its reason in the image diagnostics. Missing
+dependencies, missing configured peeled-source models, an invalid worker
+layout, cancellation and unexpected exceptions fail the task. Retries reuse Hebog's validated bundle, restore its mask, then
+repeat filtering. Keep the bundle and dual-run directories with their cycle's
+working products until restart and comparison inspection are no longer needed.
